# Credentials — never commit.
#
# These are the ordinary hygiene rules. Detection of secrets by CONTENT is
# handled by GitHub secret scanning with push protection, enabled on this
# repository: it recognises real credential material (AWS keys, RSA private
# keys, provider tokens) and blocks the push before it lands.
#
# That division matters. An earlier version of this file tried to identify
# secrets by guessing at filenames, and it could not be made to work: too broad
# and it swallowed deliveries whole (a bundle under data/tokens/ vanished, with
# every check green), too narrow and API_KEY.csv sailed through. Filename
# guessing has no floor — there is always another name.
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
*.env
.env
.env.*
config.toml
connections.toml
credentials*
rsa_key*

# Snowflake CLI local state
.snowflake/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Temporary exports
tmp/
*.tmp

# ── data/ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The delivered source files must survive `git add`. Both the manifest and the
# coverage check derive from the git index, so a delivery that git silently
# skips is invisible to every integrity gate: it never reaches Snowflake while
# CI reports green and the documentation asserts the delivery is complete.
#
# The rules above are ordinary and would swallow plausible deliveries —
# Orders.tmp, config.toml, a stray .DS_Store beside the payload. These
# re-inclusions cover the five formats actually delivered, at any depth.
#
# scripts/check-data-integrity.sh asserts this holds, including for paths inside
# directories the rules above exclude, and fails the build if a delivery would be
# invisible.
# The directory re-inclusion comes FIRST and is load-bearing. Git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so `!data/**/*.csv` alone cannot rescue a
# file inside one: a delivery under data/client_c/tmp/ or data/client_c/tokens/
# stayed invisible because `tmp/` and `credentials*` match directory names too.
# Re-including the directories lets git look inside; the extension rules then
# decide file by file.
!data/**/
!data/**/*.csv
!data/**/*.CSV
!data/**/*.xml
!data/**/*.json
!data/**/*.txt
